WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.683 --> 00:00:15.864
day Marilla said, "Diana Barry is home, Anne.

2
00:00:16.364 --> 00:00:17.865
I'm going to the Barrys' today.

3
00:00:18.365 --> 00:00:20.265
You can come with me and meet Diana."

4
00:00:20.945 --> 00:00:22.086
Anne looked up at Marilla.

5
00:00:22.106 --> 00:00:23.566
"I'm nervous!

6
00:00:24.266 --> 00:00:26.007
What if Diana doesn't like me?"

7
00:00:26.027 --> 00:00:29.588
"Diana will like you," Marilla said firmly.

8
00:00:30.252 --> 00:00:30.892
"But if Mrs.

9
00:00:30.932 --> 00:00:34.554
Barry doesn't like you, it won't matter how much Diana likes you."

10
00:00:35.514 --> 00:00:37.475
Anne and Marilla went to the Barrys' house.

11
00:00:37.495 --> 00:00:39.476
"Come in," Mrs.

12
00:00:39.536 --> 00:00:40.676
Barry said cordially.

13
00:00:40.696 --> 00:00:43.017
"Is this the girl you've adopted?"

14
00:00:43.037 --> 00:00:46.179
"Yes, this is Anne," said Marilla.

15
00:00:46.199 --> 00:00:49.160
"Spelled with an 'e'," Anne whispered.

16
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:54.422
When Diana came in, Anne saw she was a pretty girl with a happy face.

17
00:00:55.162 --> 00:00:59.800
"Diana, take Anne to the garden and show her your flowers," said Mrs.

18
00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:06.964
Barry. Outside, Anne and Diana sat among the roses, daffodils, daisies, and violets.

19
00:01:06.984 --> 00:01:09.786
"Oh, Diana," Anne blurted out.

20
00:01:09.806 --> 00:01:12.768
"Can I be your best friend?"

21
00:01:13.408 --> 00:01:14.408
Diana laughed.

22
00:01:14.428 --> 00:01:16.930
"I guess so," she said.

23
00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.351
"I'm glad you're living at Green Gables.

24
00:01:19.972 --> 00:01:24.294
There's no other girl who lives close, and my sisters are too little to play with."

25
00:01:24.314 --> 00:01:27.776
"Will you be my friend forever and ever?

26
00:01:28.464 --> 00:01:31.927
We must hold hands—like this," Anne said eagerly.

27
00:01:32.647 --> 00:01:35.569
Diana looked surprised but said, "All right."

28
00:01:35.589 --> 00:01:38.932
"I'll say the oath first," Anne said.

29
00:01:38.952 --> 00:01:46.597
"I promise to always love my dear best friend, Diana Barry, as long as the sun and moon

30
00:01:46.657 --> 00:01:47.558
are in the sky."

31
00:01:48.318 --> 00:01:50.640
Diana repeated the oath with a laugh.

32
00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:52.862
"You're a strange girl, Anne.

33
00:01:53.362 --> 00:01:55.884
But I think I'm going to like you very much!"

34
00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:59.321
The next day Anne hurried into the house.

35
00:01:59.341 --> 00:02:07.003
"Oh Marilla," she cried, "there's going to be a Sunday school picnic next Wednesday, right near the Lake

36
00:02:07.023 --> 00:02:08.384
of Shining Waters.

37
00:02:09.044 --> 00:02:09.464
And Mrs.

38
00:02:09.564 --> 00:02:11.545
Lynde is going to make ice cream.

39
00:02:12.205 --> 00:02:14.045
Think of it—ice cream!

40
00:02:14.606 --> 00:02:15.266
Can I go?"

41
00:02:15.286 --> 00:02:18.327
"Yes, of course," Marilla answered.

42
00:02:18.347 --> 00:02:21.868
"But but Anne stammered.

43
00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:26.870
"Diana says that everyone must take a basket of things to eat.

44
00:02:27.531 --> 00:02:33.254
I can't cook and—" "I'll bake something for you to bring," said Marilla.

45
00:02:33.274 --> 00:02:35.735
"Oh, you're so kind to me!"

46
00:02:36.215 --> 00:02:38.577
Anne exclaimed, kissing Marilla's cheeks.

47
00:02:39.217 --> 00:02:42.899
It was the first time in Marilla's life that a child had kissed her.

48
00:02:43.639 --> 00:02:51.063
She was secretly very pleased at Anne's impulsive show of affection, but she said gruffly, "All right, stop

49
00:02:51.083 --> 00:02:52.184
your kissing nonsense."

50
00:02:53.468 --> 00:02:59.753
It was Sunday, three days before the picnic, and Marilla wore her amethyst brooch to church, as usual.

51
00:03:00.354 --> 00:03:03.096
The brooch was Marilla's most treasured possession.

52
00:03:03.776 --> 00:03:08.160
When Anne had first seen the brooch, she'd thought it was very beautiful too.

53
00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:11.082
"Can I hold the brooch for a minute?"

54
00:03:11.603 --> 00:03:12.343
she had asked.

55
00:03:13.084 --> 00:03:16.627
"I think amethysts are sweet, like violets!"

56
00:03:17.768 --> 00:03:20.350
On Tuesday evening Marilla was frowning.

57
00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:22.932
"Have you seen my amethyst brooch?"

58
00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:24.161
she asked Anne.

59
00:03:24.181 --> 00:03:26.042
"I can't find it anywhere."

60
00:03:26.062 --> 00:03:31.746
"I saw it yesterday, when you went out," said Anne a little slowly.

61
00:03:31.766 --> 00:03:37.390
"I was passing by and I saw it, so I went to look at it."

62
00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:39.371
"Did you touch it?"

63
00:03:39.931 --> 00:03:41.232
said Marilla sternly.

64
00:03:41.252 --> 00:03:44.454
"Yes," Anne admitted hesitantly.

65
00:03:44.474 --> 00:03:47.957
"I pinned it on, just to see how it would look."

66
00:03:49.718 --> 00:03:50.919
"That was wrong, Anne.

67
00:03:51.419 --> 00:03:52.340
Where did you put it?"

68
00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:54.141
"I put it near the mirror.

69
00:03:54.661 --> 00:03:57.143
I'm sure I put it back," Anne said.

70
00:03:57.163 --> 00:04:00.525
"Well, now it's gone," said Marilla.

71
00:04:01.206 --> 00:04:03.548
She looked again, but she didn't see it anywhere.

72
00:04:03.568 --> 00:04:06.750
"Anne, you were the last person to touch it.

73
00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:09.031
Did you take the brooch and lose it?"

74
00:04:09.812 --> 00:04:11.253
"No," said Anne.

75
00:04:11.273 --> 00:04:13.775
"I never took your brooch out of the room.

76
00:04:14.255 --> 00:04:15.096
That's the truth."

77
00:04:16.557 --> 00:04:17.858
Marilla got angry.

78
00:04:17.878 --> 00:04:20.660
"I think you are lying, Anne," she said.

79
00:04:21.324 --> 00:04:25.026
"Go to your room and stay there until you are ready to confess."

80
00:04:25.046 --> 00:04:27.867
"But the picnic is tomorrow, Marilla!"

81
00:04:28.307 --> 00:04:29.107
Anne exclaimed.

82
00:04:29.127 --> 00:04:33.789
"I'll stay in my room after the picnic, but I must go to the picnic."

83
00:04:34.489 --> 00:04:38.771
"You aren't going anywhere until you confess," Marilla said firmly.

84
00:04:38.791 --> 00:04:41.932
"Oh, Marilla," gasped Anne.

85
00:04:42.392 --> 00:04:43.613
But Marilla had left.

86
00:04:44.373 --> 00:04:45.394
Marilla was worried.

87
00:04:45.974 --> 00:04:48.155
She was worried about her valuable brooch.

88
00:04:48.935 --> 00:04:50.936
She was worried that Anne told lies.

89
00:04:51.644 --> 00:04:54.225
Marilla searched the room again, but found nothing.

90
00:04:54.845 --> 00:04:57.286
Anne steadfastly refused to confess.

91
00:04:58.087 --> 00:05:01.148
Wednesday was sunny, a perfect day for a picnic.

92
00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:05.910
When Marilla took Anne her breakfast, she found Anne sitting on her bed.

93
00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:09.231
"I'm ready to confess," Anne said.

94
00:05:09.251 --> 00:05:12.573
"Ah!" Marilla said.

95
00:05:13.173 --> 00:05:16.254
Her punishment had worked, but the success was bitter.

96
00:05:16.274 --> 00:05:20.056
"I took the amethyst brooch," Anne began.

97
00:05:20.724 --> 00:05:22.105
"It was so beautiful!

98
00:05:22.745 --> 00:05:27.068
I put it on my dress and pretended I was a beautiful lady who lives in a castle.

99
00:05:27.749 --> 00:05:33.533
I went to the Lake of Shining Waters and the brooch fell off into the water and sank.

100
00:05:34.293 --> 00:05:35.934
That's my best confession."

101
00:05:36.755 --> 00:05:38.556
Marilla became very angry.

102
00:05:39.216 --> 00:05:42.779
Anne had lost her precious brooch and did not seem sorry at all!

103
00:05:42.799 --> 00:05:47.422
"Anne, you are a very wicked girl," Marilla said.

104
00:05:47.442 --> 00:05:51.448
"Yes, I suppose I am," agreed Anne.

105
00:05:51.468 --> 00:05:53.289
"You have to punish me.

106
00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:56.431
Can you punish me quickly so I can go to the picnic?"

107
00:05:57.091 --> 00:05:58.071
Marilla snorted.

108
00:05:58.091 --> 00:06:00.853
"Picnic? You're not going to the picnic.

109
00:06:01.493 --> 00:06:02.693
That is your punishment."

110
00:06:03.674 --> 00:06:04.814
Anne jumped to her feet.

111
00:06:04.834 --> 00:06:06.735
"But you promised me!

112
00:06:06.755 --> 00:06:10.577
Oh, Marilla, I must go to the picnic.

113
00:06:11.257 --> 00:06:12.878
That's why I confessed.

114
00:06:13.458 --> 00:06:14.639
Please let me go!

115
00:06:14.659 --> 00:06:16.940
There will be ice cream."

116
00:06:17.748 --> 00:06:21.110
"You're not going to the picnic and that's final!"

117
00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:22.211
Marilla said.

118
00:06:22.931 --> 00:06:27.774
Anne cried out loudly and flung herself on the bed, crying and crying.

119
00:06:27.794 --> 00:06:30.235
"I believe the child is crazy!"

120
00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:32.317
Marilla said as she left the room.

121
00:06:33.237 --> 00:06:35.939
Later Marilla decided to mend a black scarf.

122
00:06:36.619 --> 00:06:38.720
The scarf was in a box near the window.

123
00:06:39.421 --> 00:06:43.063
As Marilla held it up, something sparkled in the sunlight.

124
00:06:43.783 --> 00:06:44.744
Marilla gasped.

125
00:06:45.412 --> 00:06:49.174
It was the amethyst brooch, hanging off the end of the scarf.

126
00:06:49.194 --> 00:06:53.036
"I picked up this scarf on Monday," Marilla thought.

127
00:06:53.056 --> 00:06:56.078
"The brooch must have caught onto it."

128
00:06:57.218 --> 00:06:58.739
Marilla rushed to Anne's room.

129
00:06:58.759 --> 00:07:00.800
"I've just found my brooch.

130
00:07:01.501 --> 00:07:03.642
What story did you tell me this morning?"

131
00:07:04.382 --> 00:07:08.785
Anne replied, "You said I must stay in my room until I confessed.

132
00:07:09.625 --> 00:07:12.807
So I confessed because I wanted to go to the picnic.

133
00:07:13.487 --> 00:07:17.405
I thought of a good story, but I can't go to the picnic anyway."

134
00:07:18.465 --> 00:07:19.846
Marilla had to laugh.

135
00:07:19.866 --> 00:07:22.747
"Anne, you are a surprise!

136
00:07:23.487 --> 00:07:28.309
It was wrong for you to lie, but I understand why, and I should have believed you in

137
00:07:28.329 --> 00:07:29.050
the first place.

138
00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:32.751
So if you forgive me, I forgive you.

139
00:07:33.512 --> 00:07:35.332
Now get ready for the picnic."

140
00:07:35.352 --> 00:07:37.753
"But isn't it too late?"

141
00:07:37.773 --> 00:07:40.254
"No, it's only two o'clock.

142
00:07:40.815 --> 00:07:44.156
Wash your face and comb your hair, and I'll get some food ready."

143
00:07:45.504 --> 00:07:46.465
"Oh, Marilla!

144
00:07:47.125 --> 00:07:49.867
Five minutes ago I wished I was never born.

145
00:07:50.688 --> 00:07:53.690
Now I wouldn't change places with an angel!"

146
00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:57.833
That night Anne returned to Green Gables happy and tired.

147
00:07:57.853 --> 00:08:00.134
"It was wonderful.

148
00:08:00.694 --> 00:08:05.358
We rowed a boat, and Jane Andrews nearly fell in the lake and drowned.

149
00:08:06.098 --> 00:08:10.381
I wish it was me—how romantic to nearly drown."

150
00:08:11.242 --> 00:08:16.939
After Anne went to bed, Marilla smiled and thought, "It's never boring with Anne around."
